# Release 4.4.0

Add testing infrastructure to improve future stability as new features
are added.  This release also adds better support for the off-loading
of photons to the GPU, and handling of older DUNE GDML files.

## Notable changes since 4.3.0

* Feature: Add the ctest interface to the build system. The existing
  tests are aimed at testing the full executables, but this provides a
  base for future work.

* Feature: Update the Doke-Birks model for liquid argon so that it can
  handle the case without an electric field. The model now checks if
  an explicit Birks constant has been defined a material before
  applying the Doke-Birks model (which only applies for pure
  LAr). This helps support older DUNE GDML based geometries.

* Feature: Add support to manage externally filled (GPU-offloaded)
  photon hits. The offloading is managed through the external user
  action interface, but adding the hits to the output required some
  internal changes.

* Feature: Add the G4CutTub shape.

## Fixes since 4.3.0

* Bug Fix: Fix the Em Saturation model so that it is correctly
  initialized after the materials are initialized.

* Bug Fix: Call G4UserEventAction::EndOfEventAction in the right
  places. Previously it was only called when the event had
  ionization, which meant that "photon" only events didn't call the
  action and didn't have correct photon off-loading.

* Work-around: Add support for LArSoft GDML. This adds support for
  the LArSoft spelling of the electric field (i.e. Efield with a
  default direction along the X axis), and a way to work around
  LArSoft not specifying the electric field direction by adding the
  option EfieldDir field auxillary type. Note: The "Efield" workaround
  lacks the generality of the preferred GDML auxillary tag ("EField")
  and is provided to work around old GDML files.

* Work-around: Add support for LArSoft GDML files with partial
  material property definitions that result in the argon being state
  as either unspecified, or solid. Argon is assumed to be liquid when
  the state isn't specified. Solid argon exists, but is assumed to be
  liquid so that old GDML files work. In the future, assuming solid
  argon is liquid argon will require setting an option in the macro
  file.
